.TH SDL_SignalAsyncIOQueue 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_SignalAsyncIOQueue \- Wake up any threads that are blocking in
.BR SDL_WaitAsyncIOResult ().

.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_asyncio.h>
.PP
.BI "void SDL_SignalAsyncIOQueue(SDL_AsyncIOQueue *queue);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This will unblock any threads that are sleeping in a call to
.BR SDL_WaitAsyncIOResult
for the specified queue, and cause them to return from that function\[char46]
.PP
This can be useful when destroying a queue to make sure nothing is touching it indefinitely\[char46] In this case, once this call completes, the caller should take measures to make sure any previously-blocked threads have returned from their wait and will not touch the queue again (perhaps by setting a flag to tell the threads to terminate and then using
.BR SDL_WaitThread ()
to make sure they\(aqve done so)\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I queue
the async I/O task queue to signal\[char46]
.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_WaitAsyncIOResult (3)
